      "title": "epan: Fix unnecessary, possibly bogus or dangerous, NULL termination",
      "message": "epan: Fix unnecessary, possibly bogus or dangerous, NULL termination\n\nIn ws_label_strcpy, the label_str is always NULL terminated each time\nwe write a character. Thus, we don't need to NULL terminate at the end\nbefore returning.\n\nIt is possibly slower to NULL terminate after each character (or write\nof a run of ASCII printable in the fast path.) However, not doing so,\nand terminating at the end, requires checking to see if the position is\npast the buffer size. If it is, then rather than simply writing a NUL\nat the end of the buffer, the NUL must be written to avoid truncating\na UTF-8 multibyte character. Cf. ws_utf8_terminate.\n\nAdd some comments regarding the above so that this does get\nre-introduced.\n\nFixup ca6a8b7eff51bf32b9a880a4830c8059dd084a05\n\nFix #21511\n\nThanks to Feng Xue for the report and PoC.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
